1. STACK
    javap java.util.Stack
    -- stack is a linear data structure
    -- stack follows the principle of "last in first out".
    -- stack have three main operations
        PUSH - to insert the data in the stack
        POP -- remove or delete
        PEEK -- top most element of


    WORKING OF STACK
        -- all the operations of stack are work from single end point called top.

    CONDITIONS
        -- if TOP is == -1   i.e. the stack is empty/ underflow
        -- if top == 0,      i.e it have single element
        -- if TOP == size-1, i.e it is full/ overflow

